1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,766
A board is carried down and set where the guest law is written. The camp calls it a consultation. The house calls it a strange place to decide a river.

2
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:14,468
The question is painted in large letters. Shall the river be leased. Guests may vote. Shambhala does not vote on its own body. Nima stands with her arms folded, and with the measuring stick.

3
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:16,170
The lease fails by one. The room is very quiet, in the way of people who have been holding their breath for a year. Adler asks for a recount and is given one. The number does not move.

4
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:14,043
Captain Reza has been on duty too long. He closes a service door in the side gallery and does not bar it. He means to return in ten minutes. He sleeps for fifty.

5
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:14,043
A contractor above was told, by a man who hoped it, that the lease had passed. The contractor cuts a side tunnel toward the water, because the paperwork, he believes, is only late.

6
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:12,766
The tunnel meets the quiet aquifer. Water rises into the children's hall. It is clear. It does not roar. It comes like a tide that has been invited by nobody.

7
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:13,617
Pema is already awake. The children are lifted onto benches, then out into the school. No one drowns. The water stops at the third step, as if it has made its point.

8
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:14,043
Reza bars the door an hour after dawn. He sees the wet floor and understands the size of a missed latch. He does not ask for a softer word than the true one.

9
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:13,617
They mop. They move the beds. They do not erase the whiteboard. Sera says the vote and the flood will be taught in the same lesson, because they are the same story.

10
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:15,745
At the end of the night Sera asks the room, and the people watching this record, the same question. What would you have done at the vote. The house leaves a space where the answer would go.
